From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:55:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] include: add the power setting GUIDs and what Windows tells
 of them.

winnt.h gains the power scheme and power setting GUIDs Word registers
for (the monitor, the console display, the power source, the battery,
away mode, the idle background task, energy saver and the scheme and
its personality), SYSTEM_POWER_CONDITION, MONITOR_DISPLAY_STATE,
ENERGY_SAVER_STATUS and the platform role versions.  winuser.h gains
PBT_POWERSETTINGCHANGE and POWERBROADCAST_SETTING, powrprof.h the
callback subscription of DEVICE_NOTIFY_CALLBACK and the scheme
functions it lacked, powersetting.h the effective power mode versions
and PowerUnregisterFromEffectivePowerModeNotifications, winternl.h
THREAD_CYCLE_TIME_INFORMATION, and wtsapi32.h the NOTIFY_FOR_*
session notification flags.

libuuid defines the GUIDs of winnt.h in a file of their own: uuid.c
includes windef.h before initguid.h, which only declares them.  The
GUID values are the ones Windows answered to.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 6b0cdfe1f22b8f3cb2b84e49ce6c1b9e8a6c9083)

diff --git a/include/powersetting.h b/include/powersetting.h
index 037a04a5980..ed0622e30d2 100644
--- a/include/powersetting.h
+++ b/include/powersetting.h
@@ -36,7 +36,11 @@ typedef enum EFFECTIVE_POWER_MODE
 
 typedef void WINAPI EFFECTIVE_POWER_MODE_CALLBACK(EFFECTIVE_POWER_MODE mode, void *context);
 
+#define EFFECTIVE_POWER_MODE_V1 0x00000001
+#define EFFECTIVE_POWER_MODE_V2 0x00000002
+
 HRESULT WINAPI PowerRegisterForEffectivePowerModeNotifications(ULONG, EFFECTIVE_POWER_MODE_CALLBACK*, void*, void**);
+HRESULT WINAPI PowerUnregisterFromEffectivePowerModeNotifications(void*);
 
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
